</div><p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify; text-indent: 0.5in">The mark-to-market election
is made on a shareholder-by-shareholder basis. The mark-to-market election is made by completing Form 8621, Return by a Shareholder of
a Passive Foreign Investment Company or Qualified Electing Fund, and attaching it to the holder&#8217;s timely filed U.S. federal income
tax return for the year of election. Such election is effective for the taxable year for which made and all subsequent years until either
(a) the ordinary shares cease to be marketable stock or (b) the election is revoked with the consent of the IRS.</p><div>

</div><p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify; text-indent: 27.5pt">&#160;</p><div>

